# Capture fixtures: the exact bytes are the test.
#
# `tests/fixtures/scope-exports/` holds synthetic oscilloscope exports, and what each one
# tests is partly its byte-level shape -- one is CRLF with a trailing blank line because that
# is what an export written on Windows looks like, and the rest are LF. A checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would convert all of them in one direction or the other and quietly
# turn the corpus into nineteen copies of the same line ending.
#
# `-text` means no conversion in either direction, on any platform.
tests/fixtures/scope-exports/** -text
